            <ArticleTitle>Terbutaline inhalation for alleviation of severe pain in essential dysmenorrhea.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a double-blind cross-over study the effect of terbutaline spray (Bricanyl aerosol) inhalations was tested in 14 women with severe dysmenorrhea. A significant relief was noted in association with an increased menstrual blood loss. The side effects were few.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
